# Azure Skills Development Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your credentials
# Run `python azure-skill-generator/scripts/setup_env.py` to auto-copy and generate config
# DO NOT commit .env to version control!

# ========================================
# Environment Variable Location
# ========================================
# When working within this repo: place .env at project root
# When mixing with other Skills (AWS/JD Cloud/etc): place .env in working directory (cwd)
# Custom path: use --env-file parameter

# ========================================
# Azure API Credentials (REQUIRED)
# ========================================
# Azure RECOMMENDATION (in priority order):
#   1. Service Principal  - Use for automation (recommended)
#   2. Managed Identity   - Use when running on Azure VM/Container
#   3. Azure CLI login    - Use for local dev: `az login`
#   4. VS Code / CloudShell - Interactive development
#
# Standard Azure namespace prefix: AZURE_*

# --- Service Principal Credentials (recommended for automation) ---
# Create with: az ad sp create-for-rbac --name "my-sp" --role "Contributor" --scopes "/subscriptions/{{sub-id}}"
# Get from: Azure Portal → Microsoft Entra ID → App registrations
AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=your_subscription_id
AZURE_TENANT_ID=your_tenant_id
AZURE_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret

# ========================================
# Optional: Default Location (Region)
# ========================================
# Default: eastus
# Options: eastus, eastus2, westus, westus2, westeurope, northeurope, southeastasia, etc.
# Full list: az account list-locations --output json
AZURE_DEFAULT_LOCATION=eastus

# ========================================
# Optional: CLI Configuration
# ========================================
# Output format for az commands (json recommended for agents)
# AZURE_CLI_OUTPUT=json

# ========================================
# Optional: Development Settings
# ========================================
# Skill generation verbosity (true/false)
# SKILL_GEN_VERBOSE=false

# ========================================
# Optional: Skill Config Rendering
# ========================================
# Used by skill assets/example-config.yaml to render {{env.*}} placeholders.
# Set these so generated config examples use your actual account/region.
# AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP=my-resource-group
# AZURE_DEFAULT_VNET=vnet-xxxxx
# AZURE_DEFAULT_SUBNET=subnet-xxxxx
# AZURE_DEFAULT_VM=my-vm

# ========================================
# Priority Order (Agent Runtime)
# ========================================
# 1. Shell environment variables (highest priority)
# 2. .env file values (this file)
# 3. DefaultAzureCredential chain (Managed Identity, CLI, VS Code)
# 4. Default values (lowest priority)
#
# Example: If you set `export AZURE_DEFAULT_LOCATION=westeurope` in shell,
# it will override the value in this file.

# ========================================
# SECURITY WARNINGS
# ========================================
# 1. NEVER commit .env files to version control (.gitignore blocks this)
# 2. Use separate .env files for different environments (dev/staging/prod)
# 3. Rotate Service Principal secrets regularly (every 90 days recommended)
# 4. Grant minimal permissions to Service Principals (least privilege principle)
# 5. Never share .env files via email, chat, or any unsecured channel
# 6. Prefer Managed Identity over Service Principal when running on Azure

# ========================================
# Multi-Cloud Mixing Example (Optional)
# ========================================
# When mixing Azure Skills with other cloud provider Skills,
# use namespace prefixes to avoid credential conflicts.
#
# Example .env for multi-cloud environment:
#
# # Microsoft Azure - AZURE_* prefix
# AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=your_subscription_id
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=your_tenant_id
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
# AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret
# AZURE_DEFAULT_LOCATION=eastus
#
# # AWS - AWS_* prefix (standard)
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_aws_key
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_aws_secret
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
#
# # JD Cloud - JDC_* prefix
# JDC_ACCESS_KEY=your_jdcloud_key
# JDC_SECRET_KEY=your_jdcloud_secret
# JDC_REGION=cn-north-1
#
# # Aliyun - ALIYUN_* prefix
# ALIYUN_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_aliyun_key
# ALIYUN_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET=your_aliyun_secret
# ALIYUN_REGION=cn-hangzhou
#
# # Tencent Cloud - TENCENT_* prefix
# TENCENT_SECRET_ID=your_tencent_id
# TENCENT_SECRET_KEY=your_tencent_secret
# TENCENT_REGION=ap-guangzhou
#
# # Google Cloud Platform (GCP) - GCP_* prefix
# GCP_PROJECT_ID=your_gcp_project_id
# GCP_REGION=us-central1
# GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_PATH=/path/to/service-account-key.json
#
# # Huawei Cloud - HUAWEICLOUD_* prefix
# HUAWEICLOUD_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_access_key_id
# HUAWEICLOUD_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_secret_access_key
# HUAWEICLOUD_REGION=cn-north-4

# ========================================
# Credential Loading in Skills
# ========================================
# Agent loads credentials in the following order:
#   1. Check shell environment variables (export AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=xxx)
#   2. Check .env file in project root (this file)
#   3. Check azure-skill-generator/config.yaml (generated by setup script)
#   4. Check DefaultAzureCredential chain (Managed Identity, CLI, VS Code)
#
# The Agent MUST log each step:
#   [OK]   AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID loaded from .env
#   [SKIP] AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID not set (using DefaultAzureCredential)
#   [FAIL] No valid credential source found
#
# Error messages MUST be specific:
#   - If AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID is empty and no DefaultAzureCredential available:
#     "Azure credentials not found. Please set one of the following:
#      1. AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID + AZURE_TENANT_ID + AZURE_CLIENT_ID + AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET in .env
#      2. Run 'az login' for interactive authentication
#      3. Attach Managed Identity if running on Azure compute"
#   - If AZURE_DEFAULT_LOCATION is empty:
#     "AZURE_DEFAULT_LOCATION not set. Defaulting to eastus.
#      To change, set AZURE_DEFAULT_LOCATION in .env or shell environment."
#   - If az account show fails:
#     "Azure credential verification failed: <exact error from Azure>
#      Common causes: invalid Service Principal, expired secret, or insufficient permissions.
#      Run 'az account show' manually to diagnose."